nts"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"க்கு","gloss":"to"}],"gloss":"to suppliants"},{"surface":"அருகாது","parts":[{"text":"அருகாது","lemma":"அருகு","gloss":"without stinting"}],"gloss":"without stinting"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கொள்","parts":[{"text":"கொள்","lemma":"கொள்","gloss":"take"}],"gloss":"take"},{"surface":"என","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"என்","gloss":"saying"}],"gloss":"saying"},{"surface":"விடுவை","parts":[{"text":"விடுவை","lemma":"விடு","gloss":"you will give"}],"gloss":"you give"},{"surface":"யாயின்","parts":[{"text":"யாயின்","lemma":"யாயின்","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வெள்ளென","parts":[{"text":"வெள்","lemma":"வெண்மை","gloss":"clear"},{"text":"என","lemma":"என்","gloss":"as"}],"gloss":"clearly"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆண்டுநீ","parts":[{"text":"ஆண்டு","lemma":"ஆண்டு","gloss":"there"},{"text":"நீ","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you to that world"},{"surface":"பெயர்ந்த","parts":[{"text":"பெயர்ந்த","lemma":"பெயர்","gloss":"departed"}],"gloss":"departed"},{"surface":"பின்னும்","parts":[{"text":"பின்","lemma":"பின்","gloss":"after"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even after"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஈண்டுநீடு","parts":[{"text":"ஈண்டு","lemma":"ஈண்டு","gloss":"here"},{"text":"நீடு","lemma":"நீடு","gloss":"long time"}],"gloss":"here for a long time"},{"surface":"விளங்கும்","parts":[{"text":"விளங்கும்","lemma":"விளங்கு","gloss":"will shine"}],"gloss":"will shine"},{"surface":"நீ","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"எய்திய","parts":[{"text":"எய்திய","lemma":"எய்து","gloss":"attained"}],"gloss":"attained"},{"surface":"புகழே","parts":[{"text":"புகழ்","lemma":"புகழ்","gloss":"fame"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed the fame"}]}],"literal":"So that vultures gather, in the ruined place of many paths, / with owls of different voices and cruel mouths, / short jackals that eat corpses, having teeth glowing with fat, / ghoul women embracing and holding corpses, / having bodies smelling of strong raw flesh after eating pale flesh, / dancing by moving their feet in the cremation ground, / fearfully departing by the light of the funeral pyre, / even those who conquered countries approached the cremation ground before; / to you also, arrival of death is daily like that. / Blame will stand, and fame will stand. / Therefore, removing blame and desiring fame, / without desiring greed, speaking good things, / along with many male elephants with moonlight-like tusks, / and horses with golden ornaments crowding together, / and tall chariots shining with jewels, to suppliants without stinting, / if you give, saying take!, then clearly / even after you have departed to that world, / here for a long time will shine the fame you attained.","translation":"Even those who conquered vast lands have ultimately reached the cremation ground—a ruined place of many paths where vultures gather, where cruel-mouthed owls hoot in different voices, where short jackals with teeth glowing with fat feed on corpses, and where ghoul-women with bodies smelling of raw flesh from eating pale meat dance, moving their feet, only to depart in fear at the light of the funeral pyre. To you, too, death is certain and comes daily. Only blame and fame endure. Therefore, removing blame and desiring fame, without greed, speaking kind words, if you generously give away your many male elephants with moonlight-like tusks, your horses adorned with gold, and your tall chariots shining with jewels to suppliants, saying 'take them!', then even after you depart to the other world, the fame you attained will shine here for a long time.","modern":"பருந்துகள் கூடும் பல வழிகள் கொண்ட பாழடைந்த சுடுகாட்டில், வேறுபட்ட குரல்களை உடைய கொடிய வாயைக் கொண்ட கூகைகளுடனும், கொழுப்பு படிந்து விளங்கும் பற்களை உடைய பிணம் தின்னும் குள்ள நரிகளுடனும், வெளுத்த ஊனைத் தின்று புலால் நாற்றம் வீசும் உடம்பை உடைய பேய் மகளிர் பிணங்களைத் தழுவிப் பிடித்துக் கொண்டு, சுடுகாட்டில் கால்களை எடுத்து வைத்து ஆடி, ஈம நெருப்பின் வெளிச்சத்தைக் கண்டு அஞ்சி ஓடுவர். நாட்டை வென்ற அரசர்களும் இறுதியில் இத்தகைய சுடுகாட்டையே அடைந்தனர். உனக்கும் மரணம் வருவது ஒரு நாள் நிச்சயம். இவ்வுலகில் பழியும் நிற்கும், புகழும் நிற்கும். அதனால், பழியை நீக்கிப் புகழை விரும்பி, பேராசை கொள்ளாமல் நல்லவற்றைச் சொல்லி, நிலவு போன்ற தந்தங்களை உடைய பல ஆண் யானைகளையும், பொன்னாலான அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த குதிரைகளையும், அணிகலன்கள் விளங்கும் நெடிய தேர்களையும் இரவலர்களுக்குக் குறைவின்றி 'எடுத்துக் கொள்' என்று கொடுப்பாயானால், நீ அவ்வுலகிற்குச் சென்ற பிறகும், நீ அடைந்த புகழானது இவ்வுலகில் நெடுங்காலம் விளங்கி நிற்கும்.","explanation":"The poet Karavaṭṭaṉār addresses the chieftain Antuvaṉ Kīraṉ on the transience of life, which is the theme of Kāñci tiṇai. He begins with a vivid, eerie description of a cremation ground where vultures gather, owls hoot, jackals feed, and ghouls dance. This grim imagery serves to remind the chieftain that even the greatest conquerors who ruled vast lands eventually end up in this desolate place. Since death is inevitable and comes to everyone, the poet advises the chieftain that only fame and blame survive a person. He urges the chieftain to shun greed, speak kindly, and generously give away his elephants, horses, and chariots to suppliants so that his fame will shine long after he departs this world.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.8],[0.86,1.13],[1.19,1.6],[1.6,2.0],[2.0,3.0],[3.0,3.1],[3.1,3.1],[3.1,3.1],[3.1,5.29],[5.29,5.53],[5.53,6.5],[6.5,6.95],[7.18,7.29],[7.4,7.78],[7.85,8.5],[8.5,8.8],[8.8,9.29],[9.29,9.78],[10.27,10.6],[10.7,11.0],[11.0,11.8],[11.8,11.9],[11.9,12.85],[12.85,13.0],[13.0,13.7],[13.7,13.7],[13.7,14.55],[14.6,14.8],[14.8,15.89],[15.89,16.1],[16.1,16.8],[16.8,17.1],[17.84,18.44],[18.44,18.54],[18.54,19.14],[19.14,19.24],[19.24,19.94],[19.94,20.34],[20.34,20.74],[20.74,21.14],[21.14,21.94],[21.94,22.64],[22.64,23.34],[23.34,24.04],[24.04,24.35],[24.35,24.42],[24.42,25.36],[25.36,25.36],[25.36,25.36],[25.36,26.04],[26.27,26.94],[26.94,27